WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.650
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.320
Yume, what lesson do you want to attend today? {I know ressun is more like training, but in this episode it's irrelevant}

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.820
Today... oh, it's about time for S4 TV.{or is it S4TV}{saa}

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.460
Hello, our show is under way.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.130
S4 Presents: It's Our Job to Shine.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.840
As always, we'll be your hosts.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.340
Theater Class, Kisaragi Tsubasa...

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.840
Dance Class, Nikaidou Yuzu!

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.350
Beauty Class, Kasumi Yozora.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.100
Song Class, Shiratori Hime.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.600
We are the four glimmering stars, S4!

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.230
Our first order of business is an announcement.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:52.360
S4 has been cast in an all-new drama.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.860
A drama with S4! I'm not gonna miss that!

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.990
The producer will be none other than the top star of Theater Class, Tsubasacchi!

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:04.080
You can bet it'll have you on the edge of your seat!

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.630
We'll be recruiting extras through a schoolwide audition. {thank you for fixing this to my later change}

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.840
Schoolwide audition?

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.010
Join us in putting together a drama of utmost passion.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.510
Details can be found on the bulletin board posters!

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:23.640
I'm eager to see which darlings will be acting alongside us. {I feel as though Yozora should have something she calls her girls;}{sure;}

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.650
If you're interested, we'll be waiting for you at the auditions! {what is she doing?}{projecting, there was an episode about it}

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.770
I'm interested! I'll take the audition!

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.280
Please wait for me!

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.240
She can't hear you.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.280
It's the chance of a lifetime to act in the same drama as S4.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.780
Nijino Yume, ready to go!

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.200
I'm gonna pass that audition and act alongside S4!

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:31.060
"The story of a group of studyholic girls who formed a rock band and got into a music university on their first try."{actually, the sign is missing the 現役合格 part of what she reads. consult if you want to change swot. I randomly searched studybug and apparently that's a word too sometimes}{swot is not the acceptable. also, I want kounai audition = schoolwide audition or something like that (internal audition?)}

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.770
That's one long title!

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.770
Abbreviated, it's "Rock! Rock Girls!"

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.820
That's not an abbreviation!

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.570
It's a school rock band story.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.370
It's set at a prep school.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.410
None of the students pay attention to current trends,

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.540
and viewing their classmates as enemies in the fight for the best grades,

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.920
they focus solely on studying for their 
entrance exams, never making a single friend.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.460
But then everything changes when they form a rock band.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.720
Four friends work hard in their band

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.220
and slowly gain popularity through roadside shows.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:09.220
Eventually, they take first place at the stage of every student's dreams, Rock Koshien.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:15.980
Their band's fame nets them all scholarships into a music university.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.440
They're immortalized as the band of miracles!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.280
It's based on a bestselling novel.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.610
Wow, sounds exciting.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.200
It looks like S4 will play the main band members.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.210
But even first-years like us have the opportunity to play students of the school.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.040
I want to be in S4's drama!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.500
Rola, Koharu-chan, let's take the audition!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.760
That gets me going. Not trying would be downright un-Aikatsu!

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:45.260
I'd never make it! I've never acted in my life!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.220
Neither have I.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.470
That's all the more reason to do it.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.640
Your knowledge of the original definitely gives you an edge.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:54.770
Still...

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:59.650
Koharu-chan, if you pass the audition, 
you'll be able to act with Yozora-senpai!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.150
Act with... Yozora-senpai...

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:09.660
Well?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.790
I'll do it!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.120
All right! That's three out of three for the audition!

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.040
Let's go!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.920
That's great, but do we have any idea how to act?{you're the master of using stock translations for things that are not the thing that's stock-translated that way (そうと決まれば in this case)}{I know, it's fun}

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.720
Don't you just read lines from a script?

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.050
Huh? You think that's all there is to it?

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:34.390
Good morning! Sorry for the delay, babies.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.560
Today's foundational lesson is in acting.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.650
I've got a special instructor for you today.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.060
Instructor, come on!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.070
Tsubasa-senpai!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:52.490
Yes! At the top of Theater Class, Kisaragi Tsubasa from S4.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:55.330
She'll be teaching you the ropes of acting.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.580
That's all! Get on it!

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:04.210
I'm of the understanding that many of you will be auditioning for Rock! Rock Girls!

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:08.090
I'm holding this lesson to help those of you who lack experience.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.090
What a help!

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.100
Seriously!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.100
Now then, relocate to the lesson room.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:19.600
We'll begin with a reading of the Rock! Rock Girls! script.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.110
Okay.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.650
<i>Karejji</i>... college.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.900
<i>Bikutorii</i>... victory.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.040
Th-This is...

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:48.260
That was scene 18, where the protagonist awakens to rock.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:51.800
I think I just saw lightning strike behind Tsubasa-senpai.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.800
I even heard rock music!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.020
This is <i>real</i> acting!

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:02.690
In the next scene, the protagonist hands out flyers before school to try and recruit band members.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:06.280
However, nobody gives her a 
second glance. Let's give it a run.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.280
Please take one!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.860
N-No thank you.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.240
Your expressions and movements are stiff. Next.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.200
Please take one!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.500
No thanks!

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.170
You're walking like a robot! Next!

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.040
Acting is surprisingly stressful.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.210
I never realized how hard it is to walk naturally.{fine}

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.170
Next.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.300
Ready.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.640
Please take one!

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:35.930
Move it. {originally had "Pest"}{anything but}

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:37.640
Good.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.640
Thank you.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.520
No wonder she's the hope of Theater Class.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.400
She's in the Theater Class?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:50.280
She got the top score during the Theater Class 
sorting audition. Her name is Saotome Ako-san.{I mean I guess this is fine but it's so weird having "her name is <name>+<honorific>}

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.910
Everyone says she's the rookie with the most potential.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.700
She's a shoo-in for the audition.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.000
Saotome Ako-chan...

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:05.500
When it comes to acting, 
the Theater Class girls have an advantage.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.670
It'll be tough for the rest of us.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.550
It's too early to give up!

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:12.170
Let's do some special training before tomorrow's audition!

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.260
Special how?

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.060
So this is a studyholic?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:28.070
Those coke-bottle glasses really make it feel like she couldn't care less about fashion.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.570
Should we use makeup to look exhausted from studying? {also had exhausted, whichever works best with makeup}

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.070
Oh, now there's an idea!

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.080
S-Sorry! {piss off cunts, it's a bookstore not a library}

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.580
Subaru-kyun!

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.670
Nose deep in reference books, coke-bottle glasses,

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.760
unfashionable, exhausted-looking makeup... what else?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.800
Since everyone is an enemy, 
wouldn't that mean no friends?

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.350
Sorry...

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.100
Want some candy? {she's a kansai girl!}

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.060
Thanks. Oh, that too!

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:08.610
When you have no friends, no one gives you candy when your stomach rumbles!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.610
E-Excuse us!

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.530
That was so embarrassing...

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.490
What were you doing back there?

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.240
Back at you! What were <i>you</i> doing in there?

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.080
Just buying a book.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.090
Unfashionable, exhausted-looking makeup, doesn't get candy...

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:34.010
What do you mean, "doesn't get candy"?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.010
Looks like that set him off. {I didn'tk now this expression meant 'to have a laughing fit'}

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:41.640
Excuse me, would you mind not laughing? 
We're preparing to take S4's schoolwide audition.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:45.060
We of M4 are going to be in that drama too.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.520
What, really?

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:52.530
Hearing that not just S4, but M4 will be starring too, really raises the bar.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:57.280
But seriously, how am I supposed to act well enough?

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.280
Don't try to act well.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:00.780
What?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.830
Rookie actors are prone to get nervous and dart their eyes all around.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:08.790
So just raise your head, puff your chest out, and act confidently.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.420
Confidently?

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.550
Subaru-kun, we need to get going.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.420
Sure.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.920
See you. Good luck, Yume-chan.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.430
Act confidently...

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.180
He has a point.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.350
Aren't you... Saotome Ako-chan?

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.860
Identify yourself!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.360
Nijino Yume, we're classmates. Nice to meet you.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.740
Nijino Yume! I will most certainly not lose to you! {I thanked all the gods when she was an ojou and not a nyan nyan}{are there even any nyan nyans around anymore?}

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:42.990
Don't you forget!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.000
Why?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.220
This is Director Okamoto Jirou.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.520
Director, a few words, if you will.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.020
Drama is an explosion!

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.980
We will now begin the auditions.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.030
Come up when your number is called.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:31.170
Raise my head, puff my chest out, and act confidently.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:36.500
Okay!

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.880
It's time to announce the results of the audition.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:44.300
The passing group is... this one! {very precise}

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.100
We made it!

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:49.310
All together... Aikatsu!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:56.820
Start!

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.320
Would you consider forming a band with me?

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:04.320
Just get out of the way, 
you'll make me late for cram school.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.990
Please take one!

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.830
I'm not interested.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.000
Please take one!

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.000
A band?

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.830
How ridiculous.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.590
Cut! And okay! {...}

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:22.010
Yay, he gave us the okay!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.840
Thank goodness.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.850
Excuse me.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:34.020
Tsubasa-senpai. What did you think of our acting?

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.600
It's very much unpolished.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.360
I saw that coming.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:41.900
But you managed to stay loose and act with confidence.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.110
Not bad for your first foray.{this works goddammit don't tell me otherwise}

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.280
Thank you very much!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.870
Let's form a band together!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:56.670
What's the point of making a band? It sounds so stupid.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:01.260
I heard your dream was to become a pianist.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.880
You must really love music.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.130
That's all in the past.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.970
Piano skills contribute not a single percentage to my exam scores.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:15.140
I thought you loved rock music too... so why?

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:20.440
I must emerge victorious from the exam battlegrounds.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.530
Everyone is my enemy.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.650
Including you.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.280
Are you okay with that?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:31.620
I understand the importance of taking your exams seriously.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:35.750
But is it worth burying your own desires in an attempt to live up to your parents' expectations?

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.580
Will you truly have no regrets?

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.500
Hime-senpai is amazing.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:45.630
Everyone in S4 is such a skillful actor.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:54.810
The girls band whose popularity is skyrocketing, Rock! Rock Girls! {we could use the !!, or could say that the band name is like this but the drama name is Rock!}{I think I prefer !! but I think I don't care}

00:13:55.180 --> 00:14:00.730
It's likely they'll be our greatest rivals at Rock Koshien.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:03.070
It doesn't matter who stands in our way.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.570
We'll emerge victorious.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:08.990
M4 is so cool!

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:11.330
So they're the top boy idols.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:15.830
Yeah, but I'm an S4 fan through and through.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.840
Subaru-kyun, you're so handsome!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.420
Director, did I make a mistake?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.720
I have no issues with your acting.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.850
There's just something missing if your only trait is being cool.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:38.600
How about giving my character a girlfriend? He'll have to win for her.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.520
That's it!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:44.110
You, ribbon girl over there!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.070
Do you mean me?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.110
You're gonna play his girlfriend!

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:53.620
G-Girlfriend?

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.370
We're off the script, so just ad-lib it!

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:59.620
Ad-lib?! I-I'm not prepared!

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.250
So you can't do it?

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.090
You're not even going to try?

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:08.010
Was all that stuff about becoming an idol just talk?

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.800
Who said anything about giving up?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.350
I don't remember saying a single word of that!

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.520
But you <i>are</i> scared of failing.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:21.060
Of course I am! There isn't anybody who's not afraid of failing!

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:24.400
But if you run away because you're scared, your dream will never come true.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:28.400
As long as you don't give up and do 
your best, you'll realize your dream for sure!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.410
You're right.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:42.500
It's because you were always there for me that I've been able to come this far.

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:47.170
I'll win Rock Koshien, no matter what.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.510
Just for you.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.800
Cut! And okay!

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.970
Thank you.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.310
H-Huh? For what?

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:05.310
You got into a real groove. 
It felt like you were actually dating.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.980
Come on, don't say things like that.{pls}

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:11.320
I wouldn't get with this guy if my life depended on it.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.570
You sure know how to be rude!

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.320
You're the rude one here!

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.830
Subaru-kun, get ready for the next scene!

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:20.500
Got it. Later, boiled octopus.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.830
How many times do I need to tell you not to call me—

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.380
Th-That came out of nowhere.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:27.840
A-Ako-chan?

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.090
Don't act like we're friends!

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:33.340
How dare you... how <i>dare</i> you...

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.340
Heads up, boiled octo!

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.350
Subaru-kyun!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.220
You can have this.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:44.480
That was dangerous!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.230
Nice catch. Good luck with the rest.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.650
That guy...

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.860
Subaru-kyun gave you water...

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:52.740
Want it?

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:53.900
Really?

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.410
I-I won't accept your charity!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.500
Even if it should be water that 
Subaru-kyun touched himself...{this gives me the heebie-jeebies... like it should either be "even if it is..." or "even should it be"...}

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.750
Could it be that you like Subaru-kun?

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:09.290
Wh-What are you talking about? D-Do you have any proof?

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.000
Your face is bright red.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.260
Y-You're gravely mistaken!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.260
She's an open book.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:17.550
And this after how good she is at acting.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:18.640
She's cute.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.850
She seems like a funny girl. {eh}

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.900
It sounds like you're ready to roll, Rock Koshien!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:38.910
Next up is the girls band known for its roadside shows, Rock! Rock Girls!

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.540
Is she alone? What about the others?

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.920
Wasn't Rock! Rock Girls! a four-girl band?

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.550
Where are the other members?

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.340
There's no way we can.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.680
We didn't expect the exam and event days to overlap.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.350
What will we do for college?

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.350
Girls...

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.270
The other members are...

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:27.660
You never know your limits, leader.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.710
Not even you can be a whole band alone.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:43.720
But that's why she's our leader! 
She never, ever gives up! {GIRI GIRI AIIIIIIII}

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:55.360
I'm terrible at giving up too.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.490
You're to blame.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:03.870
It's your fault that we began to hate giving up.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:04.990
Hime...

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.120
The mock exams will come again.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:15.000
But this is the only time we'll ever get to play with our friends at Rock Koshien.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.010
Girls...

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.020
You can't sing if you cry, leader.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.270
I'm not crying!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.260
Wait, a live performance?

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.640
Are Hime-senpai and S4 seriously playing this song themselves?

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.940
Even for S4, this couldn't have been easy.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:18.020
That means they had to find time in their busy schedules to practice.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:47.180
The team that gloriously took first in Rock Koshien is...

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.930
Rock! Rock Girls!

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:03.650
What made me happiest isn't the fact that we won our battle.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:11.240
It was how I made friends who I could share my happiness and chase after my dreams with.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.960
I'm so glad! Rock! Rock Girls! rock!{ya cunt}

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:22.090
Yume, do you have to cry every time you watch a drama?

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.510
I can't help it!

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.180
Here, you can use this.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:29.220
Still, S4 was really impressive.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:31.220
Yeah, they're at a different level.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.100
This is where it begins for us!

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:37.980
Let's Aikatsu hard, just like Rock! Rock Girls!

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:38.900
Yeah.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:39.860
You got it.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:45.610
You have no chance.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.610
Oh, Ako-chan.

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:53.330
Nijino Yume! No matter how hard you 
may try, I shall always be there to crush—

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:58.380
Are you okay?

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:01.000
Yes, I'm fine. Thanks...

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:04.510
Who asked you to help me?! Hmph!

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:09.090
That's girl's so over the place it's impossible to hate her.

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:10.390
She's cute.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:13.390
Ako-chan, your acting was really awesome.

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:17.390
Of course it was! I'm going to become a great actress.

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:20.650
I know you can do it. I'll be rooting for you!

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:23.150
Your assistance is unnecessary!

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:01.080
Catch the fresh first-years' acting.

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:04.250
The band's coords were Spice Chord's Season Dresses.

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:09.050
Critics everywhere are raving about how touching the interplay of the music and story was.

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:13.010
What is it that makes me unique?! {I'll let this slide for now, but next episode it's going right back}

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.600
Rola left on a journey to find herself?{timing}

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:18.770
Hey, hurry up and come back!

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:20.520
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:22.020
Simple is the Best.

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:24.480
Become the first-star idol!
